    type: string
    description: >-
      Agreed allocation of receipts and performance obligations: the relevant periods,
      dates/times/time zones and any straddle-period rule, and the allocation that applies to each
      Schedule C item. This does not set Closing, transfer title or satisfy operational acceptance;
      tax and price-adjustment measurement rules are stated separately. No inferred effective time.
    section: Transaction
  - name: purchase_price_amount
    type: string
    description: Amount and currency
    section: Transaction
  - name: payment_instructions
    type: string
    description: Recipient, method and payment timing
    section: Transaction
  - name: governing_law
    type: string
    description: Governing jurisdiction
    section: Transaction
  - name: dispute_process
    type: string
    description: Forum, procedure and interim relief
    section: Transaction
  - name: buyer_notice_address
    type: string
    description: Address, email and notice recipient
    section: Transaction
  - name: seller_notice_address
    type: string
    description: Address, email and notice recipient
    section: Transaction
  - name: notice_effectiveness
    type: string
    description: Agreed delivery and receipt rules, including electronic failure and nonbusiness days.
    section: Transaction
  - name: tax_allocation
    type: string
    description: >-
      Transfer-tax responsibility, reporting allocation process, timing and dispute process; each
      depends on jurisdiction-specific review.
    section: Transaction
  - name: schedule_assets
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule A: item ID, asset description, owner, acquired right, version/identifier, location
      and transfer instrument. Schedule A covers only owned rights or identified transferable
      licenses.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_exclusions
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule B: excluded assets, personal/shared accounts, retained code/content/data and
      dependencies; specify none affirmatively if none.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_liabilities
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule C: each assumed liability, relevant contract/order/cohort, amount or method, cutoff
      and exclusions; prepayments, refunds, chargebacks, credits, taxes and costs are allocated
      separately. If there are none, the schedule says so affirmatively.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_transfers
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule D: each domain/account/contract/license, provider/registrant, applicable transfer
      restrictions, required consents, permitted method, responsible party, deadline and
      missing-consent election. Linked billing and recovery dependencies are listed without
      secrets.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_deliverables
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule E: each closing instrument and technical deliverable, classification as
      closing-condition, escrow-release-condition or post-closing-obligation, responsible party, due
      date, affirmative test, reviewer, evidence, defect notice, cure, retest and failure
      consequence. Distinguish source code from deployed build and submitted from approved versions.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_disclosures
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule F: dated disclosures keyed to the affected representation, exceptions, known claims,
      incidents and incomplete ownership or consent evidence; specify none affirmatively where
      appropriate.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_revenue
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule G: historical measurement periods, gross/net/recurring definitions, currency,
      refunds, fees, taxes, nonrecurring items, source exports and reconciliation differences;
      identify agreed figures and exceptions.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_priority
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule H: each related instrument by parties/date/version, incorporated or continuing
      provisions, express conflict priority and any amendment; include broker and escrow obligations
      if relevant.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_data
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule I: transferred data categories, purposes, permissions/notices, retention limits,
      lawful migration route, safeguards, incident handling and seller retained-copy basis and
      deletion dates.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_transition
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule J: services, responsible personnel, hours, response windows, start/end, costs, access
      limits, documentation, escalation and exit.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_remedies
    type: string
    description: >-
      Schedule K: liability survival by claim category, caps and exceptions, thresholds, recovery
      limits, exclusivity, fraud treatment and setoff election; state expressly whether each
      limitation applies or does not apply.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_adjustment
    type: string
    description: >-
      Adjustment terms: baseline and closing measurement, accounting rules/hierarchy, statements,
      access, objections, independent determination and payment dates.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_earnout
    type: string
    description: >-
      Earnout terms: metric, accounting rules, periods, cap if agreed, operating obligations,
      reporting/access, objections, independent determination, payment and acceleration/effect of
      resale or discontinuation.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_escrow
    type: string
    description: >-
      Escrow/holdback terms: agent or holder, funding amount/timing, release tests/dates,
      objections, disputed reserve, partial release, fees, interest and controlling signed
      instructions.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_indemnity
    type: string
    description: >-
      Indemnity allocation: indemnifying parties, covered claims/losses, retained/assumed liability
      allocation, beneficiaries and interaction with Schedule K.
    section: Schedules
  - name: schedule_claims
    type: string
    description: >-
      Claims process: notice, required detail, response time, defense control and conflicts,
      counsel/costs, cooperation, settlement consent, direct claims and payment.
    section: Schedules
